  "content": "---\ntitle: Reading notes (secondary)\nauthor: Jo (invented; sample)\n---\n\n## Sharon Cameron, *Choosing Not Choosing: Dickinson's Fascicles* (1992)\n\nThe book about variants. Her argument, as I understand it: the variant words in the fascicles aren't drafts waiting for a decision, they're part of the poem; Dickinson keeps the alternatives open on purpose. \"Choosing not choosing.\" I read the introduction and the chapter that deals with the fascicle context. This is the idea the piece is arguing with: a press can't not choose.\n\n## Susan Howe, *My Emily Dickinson* (1985)\n\nLess about this poem than about how editors flattened her. Howe is angry at the way the manuscripts were regularized. Useful for the colophon problem: I also regularized her, in metal. There's no dash sort that matches her marks.\n\n## Cristanne Miller, ed., *Emily Dickinson's Poems: As She Preserved Them* (2016)\n\nThe edition I used for the texts alongside the Archive images. Prints the fascicle versions with the variants listed. Her note on Fr124 lays out the versions and the exchange with Sue.\n\n## Marta Werner and Jen Bervin, *The Gorgeous Nothings* (2013)\n\nThe envelope poems, facsimile. Not this poem, but it's where I got the idea that the shape of the paper is part of the writing. The broadside format comes from looking at this.\n\n## Still to read\n\nWerner's *Open Folios* (1995). Domhnall Mitchell on the manuscripts. Whatever Marta Werner has said about \"Alabaster\" specifically.\n"
